1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:07,916
What's today's video about? Onomatopoeia! Exciting, isn't it?

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Dealing with Cold Symptoms

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:13,914
What's wrong?

4
00:00:13,937 --> 00:00:16,826
You don't look well.

5
00:00:16,849 --> 00:00:20,216
I'm not feeling too great.

6
00:00:20,239 --> 00:00:22,306
Are you okay?

7
00:00:22,329 --> 00:00:24,862
Do you have a fever?

8
00:00:24,885 --> 00:00:27,918
I don't think I have a fever.

9
00:00:27,941 --> 00:00:32,275
But my head is pounding.

10
00:00:32,298 --> 00:00:34,798
That sounds rough.

11
00:00:34,821 --> 00:00:37,654
You might have a cold.

12
00:00:37,677 --> 00:00:40,323
Maybe so.

13
00:00:40,347 --> 00:00:44,113
I've felt a bit chilly since yesterday.

14
00:00:44,136 --> 00:00:47,336
You should take a rest.

15
00:00:47,359 --> 00:00:48,893
Okay.

16
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:52,955
But I feel dizzy when I stand up.

17
00:00:52,979 --> 00:00:55,389
Don't push yourself.

18
00:00:55,412 --> 00:01:00,264
Shall I get you some medicine?

19
00:01:00,288 --> 00:01:01,890
I'm sorry to trouble you.

20
00:01:01,913 --> 00:01:04,365
Here you go.

21
00:01:04,388 --> 00:01:07,081
I'll leave some water here too.

22
00:01:07,105 --> 00:01:08,771
Thank you.

23
00:01:08,794 --> 00:01:10,761
That really helps.

24
00:01:10,784 --> 00:01:14,117
Anywhere else hurting?

25
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:18,818
Actually, my tooth is throbbing a bit too.

26
00:01:18,842 --> 00:01:21,448
That must be tough.

27
00:01:21,472 --> 00:01:24,686
You should see a dentist too.

28
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:26,876
You're right.

29
00:01:26,899 --> 00:01:31,034
I'll rest this afternoon and go to the hospital.

30
00:01:31,057 --> 00:01:34,591
I'll let the manager know for you.

31
00:01:34,614 --> 00:01:36,880
I'm really sorry about this.

32
00:01:36,903 --> 00:01:38,575
Please do.

33
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:40,999
Don't worry about it.

34
00:01:41,022 --> 00:01:44,100
Health is the most important thing.

35
00:01:44,124 --> 00:01:45,572
Okay.

36
00:01:45,595 --> 00:01:48,482
Yes, I think I'll be better by tomorrow.

37
00:01:48,505 --> 00:01:51,393
Shall I call a taxi for you?

38
00:01:51,417 --> 00:01:52,686
Okay.

39
00:01:52,710 --> 00:01:54,376
Please do.

40
00:01:54,399 --> 00:01:58,333
I just ordered one using my smartphone app.

41
00:01:58,356 --> 00:02:00,036
Thank you.

42
00:02:00,059 --> 00:02:04,593
It'll be here in about 5 minutes, in front of the office.

43
00:02:04,616 --> 00:02:06,782
I'll gather my things.

44
00:02:06,805 --> 00:02:09,805
Let me carry your bag.

45
00:02:09,828 --> 00:02:13,509
I'm really sorry for all this trouble.

46
00:02:13,533 --> 00:02:17,699
Take care. Get plenty of rest.

47
00:02:17,722 --> 00:02:19,522
Thank you.

48
00:02:19,545 --> 00:02:21,712
Excuse me.

49
00:02:21,735 --> 00:02:23,235
Scene 2: Wrapping Up Work and Dinner Plans

50
00:02:23,235 --> 00:02:27,568
We're done with work for today, right?

51
00:02:27,591 --> 00:02:30,658
Yes, I'm exhausted.

52
00:02:30,681 --> 00:02:33,648
I'm completely wiped out.

53
00:02:33,671 --> 00:02:36,485
We walked a lot today.

54
00:02:36,508 --> 00:02:39,108
We sure did.

55
00:02:39,131 --> 00:02:42,331
My feet are killing me.

56
00:02:42,354 --> 00:02:47,320
Would you like to grab dinner together later?

57
00:02:47,343 --> 00:02:49,277
That sounds great!

58
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:52,199
I'm starving.

59
00:02:52,222 --> 00:02:55,622
Is there anything you're craving?

60
00:02:55,645 --> 00:02:58,978
I'd love some meat.

61
00:02:59,001 --> 00:03:03,854
There's a delicious yakiniku place nearby.

62
00:03:03,878 --> 00:03:05,811
Let's go there.

63
00:03:05,834 --> 00:03:08,167
I want to eat a lot.

64
00:03:08,190 --> 00:03:10,957
I'm thirsty too.

65
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:14,713
Yeah, my throat is parched.

66
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:17,976
Shall we get some cold beer?

67
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,366
I'll have tea instead.

68
00:03:20,389 --> 00:03:23,757
Aren't you drinking alcohol today?

69
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:27,647
No, I drove here today.

70
00:03:27,670 --> 00:03:30,470
Oh, right.

71
00:03:30,493 --> 00:03:32,826
I completely forgot.

72
00:03:32,849 --> 00:03:36,651
Is the yakiniku place far from here?

73
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:40,008
It's about a 10-minute walk.

74
00:03:40,031 --> 00:03:42,198
Oh, that's close.

75
00:03:42,221 --> 00:03:46,487
But it's always packed on Fridays.

76
00:03:46,510 --> 00:03:49,001
Did you make a reservation?

77
00:03:49,025 --> 00:03:51,358
No, I didn't.

78
00:03:51,381 --> 00:03:54,615
Should I call them now?

79
00:03:54,638 --> 00:03:56,004
You're right.

80
00:03:56,027 --> 00:03:58,279
I'll give them a call.

81
00:03:58,303 --> 00:04:00,103
Please do.

82
00:04:00,126 --> 00:04:02,759
Hope they have seats available.

83
00:04:02,782 --> 00:04:07,315
Hello, do you have space for two right now?

84
00:04:07,338 --> 00:04:09,105
Okay.

85
00:04:09,128 --> 00:04:10,605
Okay.

86
00:04:10,628 --> 00:04:12,833
We got a reservation!

87
00:04:12,857 --> 00:04:15,390
Great!

88
00:04:15,413 --> 00:04:17,613
Let's hurry.

89
00:04:17,636 --> 00:04:20,325
Yeah, I'm excited!

90
00:04:20,348 --> 00:04:21,848
Scene 3: Reflections on the Speech Contest

91
00:04:21,848 --> 00:04:26,182
You did great at the speech contest. Well done!

92
00:04:26,205 --> 00:04:28,005
Thank you.

93
00:04:28,028 --> 00:04:30,594
It's finally over.

94
00:04:30,617 --> 00:04:33,951
Your speech was amazing!

95
00:04:33,973 --> 00:04:36,046
Really?

96
00:04:36,070 --> 00:04:39,003
I made a few mistakes.

97
00:04:39,026 --> 00:04:42,259
I didn’t notice at all!

98
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:44,559
You were really good.

99
00:04:44,583 --> 00:04:48,383
My heart was pounding before it started.

100
00:04:48,406 --> 00:04:52,039
There were so many people.

101
00:04:52,062 --> 00:04:54,315
You were nervous, huh?

102
00:04:54,339 --> 00:04:57,906
I forgot my next line at one point.

103
00:04:57,929 --> 00:05:01,574
You paused for a moment.

104
00:05:01,598 --> 00:05:04,998
I was on the edge of my seat, worried you'd mess up.

105
00:05:05,021 --> 00:05:08,512
I was a little worried too.

106
00:05:08,535 --> 00:05:12,737
But you made it to the end.

107
00:05:12,761 --> 00:05:15,494
That’s really great.

108
00:05:15,517 --> 00:05:17,520
You did an excellent job.

109
00:05:17,543 --> 00:05:21,680
Now that it's over, I feel so relieved.

110
00:05:21,704 --> 00:05:24,304
I'm relieved too.

111
00:05:24,327 --> 00:05:28,168
Yes, I feel like a weight has been lifted off my shoulders.

112
00:05:28,192 --> 00:05:30,959
Did your family come to watch?

113
00:05:30,982 --> 00:05:35,715
Yes, my parents were sitting in the front row.

114
00:05:35,738 --> 00:05:39,538
I’m sure your parents are happy for you.

115
00:05:39,561 --> 00:05:43,294
We’re going to have a meal together afterward.

116
00:05:43,317 --> 00:05:45,351
That’s wonderful.

117
00:05:45,374 --> 00:05:47,907
What are you going to eat?

118
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:50,663
We’re going out for sushi.

119
00:05:50,686 --> 00:05:52,622
That sounds great!

120
00:05:52,645 --> 00:05:55,612
This is all thanks to you.

121
00:05:55,635 --> 00:06:00,002
Oh no, I didn’t do anything.

122
00:06:00,025 --> 00:06:03,834
You kept me company every day during practice.

123
00:06:03,857 --> 00:06:07,224
It’s because of all the hard work *you* put in.

124
00:06:07,247 --> 00:06:12,214
Next time, I’ll tackle an even more challenging theme.

125
00:06:12,237 --> 00:06:14,570
I’m looking forward to it.

126
00:06:14,593 --> 00:06:17,476
Make sure to rest well today.

127
00:06:17,499 --> 00:06:20,954
Yes, thank you.

128
00:06:20,977 --> 00:06:22,477
Scene 4: Delayed Train and Anxiety

129
00:06:22,477 --> 00:06:25,044
What’s wrong?

130
00:06:25,067 --> 00:06:28,433
The train just won’t come.

131
00:06:28,456 --> 00:06:31,862
The train just won’t come.

132
00:06:31,886 --> 00:06:34,920
I heard there was an accident.

133
00:06:34,943 --> 00:06:37,402
Really?

134
00:06:37,425 --> 00:06:40,391
I had no idea.

135
00:06:40,414 --> 00:06:43,669
It’s running about 30 minutes late.

136
00:06:43,693 --> 00:06:47,826
It’s so frustrating—what a waste of time.

137
00:06:47,849 --> 00:06:50,260
Are you in a hurry?

138
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:51,693
Okay.

139
00:06:51,717 --> 00:06:56,150
I’m supposed to meet a friend to watch a movie.

140
00:06:56,173 --> 00:06:59,467
Will you make it in time?

141
00:06:59,491 --> 00:07:02,825
Probably not.

142
00:07:02,848 --> 00:07:05,814
Did you contact your friend?

143
00:07:05,837 --> 00:07:07,071
Okay.

144
00:07:07,094 --> 00:07:10,060
I just sent them a message.

145
00:07:10,083 --> 00:07:13,287
What did they say?

146
00:07:13,311 --> 00:07:17,477
They said they’d go ahead and get into the theater.

147
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:20,334
Was it a movie you were really looking forward to?

148
00:07:20,357 --> 00:07:21,890
Okay.

149
00:07:21,913 --> 00:07:25,356
It’s an action movie I’ve been wanting to see for ages.

150
00:07:25,379 --> 00:07:29,979
It’s disappointing that you’ll miss the beginning.

151
00:07:30,002 --> 00:07:33,038
It’s really too bad.

152
00:07:33,062 --> 00:07:36,495
When’s the next train coming?

153
00:07:36,518 --> 00:07:40,318
The board doesn’t say.

154
00:07:40,341 --> 00:07:43,775
Should we ask the station attendant?

155
00:07:43,798 --> 00:07:45,231
You're right.

156
00:07:45,254 --> 00:07:48,621
There’s one over there.

157
00:07:48,644 --> 00:07:51,010
I’ll go ask.

158
00:07:51,033 --> 00:07:53,211
What did they say?

159
00:07:53,235 --> 00:07:57,251
They said it’ll start moving in about 10 minutes.

160
00:07:57,274 --> 00:07:59,755
That’s a relief.

161
00:07:59,778 --> 00:08:02,916
Does that ease your mind a little?

162
00:08:02,939 --> 00:08:04,551
Okay.

163
00:08:04,575 --> 00:08:06,775
Yeah, I feel a bit better now.

164
00:08:06,798 --> 00:08:10,401
Hope you enjoy the movie!

165
00:08:10,425 --> 00:08:12,192
Thank you.

166
00:08:12,215 --> 00:08:14,551
I’m off!

167
00:08:14,574 --> 00:08:16,074
Scene 5: Winter Vacation Travel Plans

168
00:08:16,074 --> 00:08:19,874
Winter break starts tomorrow!

169
00:08:19,897 --> 00:08:23,555
Yes, I can't wait!

170
00:08:23,578 --> 00:08:27,180
Do you have any plans to go somewhere?

171
00:08:27,204 --> 00:08:31,048
I'm going to Hokkaido with my family.

172
00:08:31,071 --> 00:08:35,405
Hokkaido? That sounds amazing!

173
00:08:35,428 --> 00:08:40,228
It's my first time in a snowy place, so I'm really excited.

174
00:08:40,251 --> 00:08:43,017
It's going to be really cold, though.

175
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:46,174
Did you buy some warm clothes?

176
00:08:46,196 --> 00:08:51,130
Yes, I got a new warm coat.

177
00:08:51,153 --> 00:08:56,019
New clothes always make me happy, don't they?

178
00:08:56,042 --> 00:08:59,976
Yeah, I can't wait to wear it.

179
00:08:59,999 --> 00:09:03,696
What are you planning to do in Hokkaido?

180
00:09:03,719 --> 00:09:06,652
I'm going to try skiing.

181
00:09:06,675 --> 00:09:09,528
Are you good at skiing?

182
00:09:09,552 --> 00:09:12,236
Not at all.

183
00:09:12,259 --> 00:09:14,926
It's my first time.

184
00:09:14,949 --> 00:09:17,949
I'm sure you'll have a great time.

185
00:09:17,972 --> 00:09:20,705
The snow is so beautiful, too.

186
00:09:20,728 --> 00:09:24,095
I also want to try the delicious seafood bowls.

187
00:09:24,118 --> 00:09:27,684
The crab and salmon are amazing there.

188
00:09:27,707 --> 00:09:32,742
Just talking about it makes me restless—I can't wait to go!

189
00:09:32,766 --> 00:09:37,203
I can't focus on work at all today.

190
00:09:37,227 --> 00:09:40,793
Yeah, I keep checking the clock.

191
00:09:40,816 --> 00:09:45,050
Did you check your flight ticket yet?

192
00:09:45,073 --> 00:09:47,917
Of course, I did.

193
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:51,274
Is your hotel reservation all set?

194
00:09:51,297 --> 00:09:54,697
Yes, everything's perfect.

195
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:58,686
Don't forget to bring your camera!

196
00:09:58,709 --> 00:10:02,143
I'll take lots of photos with my smartphone.

197
00:10:02,166 --> 00:10:05,932
I'm looking forward to seeing the beautiful pictures.

198
00:10:05,955 --> 00:10:08,931
I'll show you on Monday.

199
00:10:08,954 --> 00:10:11,621
Have a safe trip!

200
00:10:11,644 --> 00:10:13,777
Thanks, I'll be off now.

201
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:16,979
I'll bring you back a souvenir.

202
00:10:17,003 --> 00:10:18,503
Scene 6: Sleep and Morning Feelings

203
00:10:18,503 --> 00:10:20,923
Good morning.

204
00:10:20,946 --> 00:10:23,313
Good morning.

205
00:10:23,336 --> 00:10:26,912
You're earlier than usual this morning.

206
00:10:26,935 --> 00:10:31,203
I went to bed really early yesterday.

207
00:10:31,227 --> 00:10:34,270
Did you sleep well?

208
00:10:34,293 --> 00:10:38,500
Yes, I didn't wake up once until morning.

209
00:10:38,523 --> 00:10:41,490
That's great!

210
00:10:41,513 --> 00:10:46,148
I feel so refreshed this morning.

211
00:10:46,171 --> 00:10:48,987
You look really energetic.

212
00:10:49,010 --> 00:10:53,377
Yeah. You look a bit sleepy, though.

213
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:58,499
Actually, I was playing games late into the night.

214
00:10:58,522 --> 00:11:01,016
How many hours did you sleep?

215
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:04,138
About three hours.

216
00:11:04,161 --> 00:11:07,096
That's way too little!

217
00:11:07,119 --> 00:11:09,160
It's bad for your health.

218
00:11:09,184 --> 00:11:14,080
Yeah, I dozed off during the meeting earlier.

219
00:11:14,103 --> 00:11:16,377
Really?

220
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:19,376
Did the manager notice?

221
00:11:19,399 --> 00:11:22,933
I think it was probably okay.

222
00:11:22,956 --> 00:11:26,089
You should be careful, though.

223
00:11:26,112 --> 00:11:30,967
I want to go home early after work today.

224
00:11:30,991 --> 00:11:34,924
Have you finished work for today?

225
00:11:34,947 --> 00:11:39,081
I still have a bit of paperwork left to do.

226
00:11:39,105 --> 00:11:42,305
Need a hand with that?

227
00:11:42,328 --> 00:11:44,506
Really?

228
00:11:44,530 --> 00:11:46,730
That would be a huge help!

229
00:11:46,753 --> 00:11:49,919
Which document should I work on?

230
00:11:49,942 --> 00:11:55,014
Please enter this paper data into the computer.

231
00:11:55,038 --> 00:11:57,238
Got it.

232
00:11:57,261 --> 00:11:59,297
I'll get right on it.

233
00:11:59,321 --> 00:12:03,254
I'll take care of the email replies.

234
00:12:03,277 --> 00:12:07,410
Let's head home together once we're done.

235
00:12:07,434 --> 00:12:09,000
Thank you.

236
00:12:09,023 --> 00:12:13,362
Make sure to get a good long sleep tonight, okay?

237
00:12:13,386 --> 00:12:14,886
Scene 7: Moving Day Prep Complete

238
00:12:14,886 --> 00:12:19,539
The move is finally this weekend!

239
00:12:19,562 --> 00:12:25,204
Yeah, packing has been quite a task.

240
00:12:25,227 --> 00:12:29,561
Want me to come help out?

241
00:12:29,584 --> 00:12:31,476
No need, I'm good.

242
00:12:31,499 --> 00:12:33,632
I'm almost done, actually.

243
00:12:33,655 --> 00:12:37,388
Is the room all tidied up?

244
00:12:37,411 --> 00:12:41,095
It was a total mess until yesterday.

245
00:12:41,119 --> 00:12:46,252
The longer you live somewhere, the more stuff you accumulate.

246
00:12:46,275 --> 00:12:50,808
I threw out all the old magazines.

247
00:12:50,831 --> 00:12:54,198
What did you do with the clothes you didn't need?

248
00:12:54,221 --> 00:12:57,871
I tossed the worn-out ones.

249
00:12:57,894 --> 00:13:02,461
The ones still in good shape can be recycled, you know.

250
00:13:02,484 --> 00:13:06,954
Yep, I took them to a recycling shop.

251
00:13:06,977 --> 00:13:09,251
That's great!

252
00:13:09,275 --> 00:13:11,908
The room feels so much more spacious now.

253
00:13:11,932 --> 00:13:16,865
I don't have much to take to the new apartment.

254
00:13:16,888 --> 00:13:21,708
What's your new place like?

255
00:13:21,731 --> 00:13:27,664
It's brand new—floors and walls are sparkling!

256
00:13:27,687 --> 00:13:30,654
That sounds exciting!

257
00:13:30,677 --> 00:13:35,410
The windows are huge, so it's really bright.

258
00:13:35,433 --> 00:13:38,052
Is it close to the station?

259
00:13:38,075 --> 00:13:41,285
Just a five-minute walk.

260
00:13:41,308 --> 00:13:44,708
That'll make your commute so much easier!

261
00:13:44,731 --> 00:13:48,538
There's a big supermarket nearby too.

262
00:13:48,562 --> 00:13:53,129
Sounds like a really convenient place to live—I'm jealous!

263
00:13:53,152 --> 00:13:56,765
You should come visit next month!

264
00:13:56,788 --> 00:13:59,521
I'd love to!

265
00:13:59,544 --> 00:14:04,077
I'll have some delicious cake ready for you.

266
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:07,867
I'll bring a housewarming gift.

267
00:14:07,890 --> 00:14:09,569
Thank you.

268
00:14:09,592 --> 00:14:13,047
Is there anything you need?

269
00:14:13,071 --> 00:14:16,404
I could use some new dishes.

270
00:14:16,427 --> 00:14:17,927
Scene 8: Chatting on a Rainy Day

271
00:14:17,927 --> 00:14:21,809
The sky suddenly got so dark.

272
00:14:21,833 --> 00:14:25,452
Those black clouds are rolling in.

273
00:14:25,475 --> 00:14:28,409
It might rain soon.

274
00:14:28,432 --> 00:14:31,865
Oh, a cold wind just blew in.

275
00:14:31,888 --> 00:14:34,964
It's really pouring now, isn't it?

276
00:14:34,987 --> 00:14:37,721
Do you have an umbrella?

277
00:14:37,744 --> 00:14:41,277
No, I didn’t bring one today.

278
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:45,533
I have a big foldable umbrella.

279
00:14:45,556 --> 00:14:48,416
Mind if I share it with you?

280
00:14:48,439 --> 00:14:51,493
Of course, go ahead!

281
00:14:51,516 --> 00:14:53,317
Thank you.

282
00:14:53,341 --> 00:14:55,108
You’re a lifesaver!

283
00:14:55,131 --> 00:14:59,764
But the wind’s so strong, we’re still getting a little wet.

284
00:14:59,787 --> 00:15:03,157
Yeah, my shoes are soaked.

285
00:15:03,181 --> 00:15:07,030
Be careful—the ground’s slippery.

286
00:15:07,053 --> 00:15:10,720
Did you see that flash in the sky earlier?

287
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:13,642
Yeah, that’s thunder.

288
00:15:13,666 --> 00:15:16,868
Listen, it’s rumbling now.

289
00:15:16,892 --> 00:15:20,303
That’s a loud one… scary, isn’t it?

290
00:15:20,326 --> 00:15:23,532
We should find somewhere safe.

291
00:15:23,555 --> 00:15:26,389
There’s a convenience store over there!

292
00:15:26,412 --> 00:15:28,579
Let’s make a run for it!

293
00:15:28,602 --> 00:15:29,936
Okay.

294
00:15:29,959 --> 00:15:32,893
We made it just in time!

295
00:15:32,916 --> 00:15:36,482
My clothes got a little wet, though.

296
00:15:36,505 --> 00:15:38,804
Should we grab a towel?

297
00:15:38,827 --> 00:15:42,843
Good idea—I don’t want to catch a cold.

298
00:15:42,866 --> 00:15:45,800
Let’s get some hot coffee too.

299
00:15:45,823 --> 00:15:49,261
Sounds perfect—I’m a little chilly.

300
00:15:49,284 --> 00:15:52,099
I wonder when this rain will stop.

301
00:15:52,123 --> 00:15:56,256
Let’s just wait here until the weather clears up.

302
00:15:56,279 --> 00:15:57,779
Scene 9: First Time at a Café – A Taste of Delight

303
00:15:57,779 --> 00:16:01,648
Is this your first time at this café?

304
00:16:01,672 --> 00:16:05,117
Yeah, it’s my first time here.

305
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:08,540
Their pancakes are famous, you know.

306
00:16:08,563 --> 00:16:12,530
The pictures on the menu look so delicious!

307
00:16:12,553 --> 00:16:16,927
The batter is fluffy—absolutely amazing.

308
00:16:16,950 --> 00:16:20,601
Then I’ll order that!

309
00:16:20,625 --> 00:16:23,825
I think I’ll go with a croissant.

310
00:16:23,848 --> 00:16:26,849
Are the croissants good too?

311
00:16:26,872 --> 00:16:30,539
Yeah, the outside is crispy.

312
00:16:30,562 --> 00:16:33,695
The sound and texture are perfect.

313
00:16:33,718 --> 00:16:38,451
And the inside smells so buttery.

314
00:16:38,474 --> 00:16:41,810
How about this tapioca milk tea?

315
00:16:41,834 --> 00:16:46,201
The tapioca pearls are chewy—it’s really popular.

316
00:16:46,224 --> 00:16:49,424
Then I’ll get that for my drink.

317
00:16:49,447 --> 00:16:52,447
We ordered a lot, didn’t we?

318
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:56,603
I’m *so* hungry today.

319
00:16:56,626 --> 00:17:00,426
Excuse me, could we place our order?

320
00:17:00,449 --> 00:17:03,024
Now let’s wait and enjoy the anticipation!

321
00:17:03,047 --> 00:17:06,647
Oh, the pancakes are here!

322
00:17:06,670 --> 00:17:09,961
Wow, they’re so thick!

323
00:17:09,985 --> 00:17:14,059
Let’s drown them in syrup.

324
00:17:14,083 --> 00:17:15,572
Time to dig in!

325
00:17:15,596 --> 00:17:17,862
How does it taste?

326
00:17:17,885 --> 00:17:20,940
It melts in your mouth.

327
00:17:20,964 --> 00:17:23,497
It's really soft.

328
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:26,322
I'm so glad I liked it.

329
00:17:26,346 --> 00:17:29,779
Can I have a bite of the croissant too?

330
00:17:29,802 --> 00:17:32,606
Here you go.

331
00:17:32,630 --> 00:17:35,764
It's so crispy!

332
00:17:35,787 --> 00:17:39,590
Next time, let's try a different cake.

333
00:17:39,613 --> 00:17:43,213
Yes, I definitely want to come back again.

334
00:17:43,236 --> 00:17:44,736
Scene 10: Characteristics of the New Part-Timer

335
00:17:44,736 --> 00:17:48,836
How's the new part-timer doing?

336
00:17:48,859 --> 00:17:51,226
Are you talking about Suzuki?

337
00:17:51,249 --> 00:17:54,103
Yes, that's right.

338
00:17:54,126 --> 00:17:56,692
He's very diligent.

339
00:17:56,715 --> 00:18:00,482
Does he pick up work quickly?

340
00:18:00,505 --> 00:18:04,547
No, he's a bit laid-back.

341
00:18:04,570 --> 00:18:06,971
I see.

342
00:18:06,995 --> 00:18:10,962
But he never makes mistakes.

343
00:18:10,985 --> 00:18:14,163
That's wonderful.

344
00:18:14,186 --> 00:18:18,262
He works steadily every day.

345
00:18:18,285 --> 00:18:23,018
Taking care with your work is important.

346
00:18:23,041 --> 00:18:25,975
He takes a lot of notes too.

347
00:18:25,998 --> 00:18:29,398
He's so responsible for his age.

348
00:18:29,421 --> 00:18:32,387
I really admire that.

349
00:18:32,410 --> 00:18:36,377
How was Sato, the one who was here before?

350
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:40,877
Sato was very fast at work.

351
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:44,149
But he made a lot of mistakes.

352
00:18:44,173 --> 00:18:45,856
You're right.

353
00:18:45,879 --> 00:18:49,412
He often got scolded by customers.

354
00:18:49,435 --> 00:18:53,602
Suzuki is much more reassuring to watch.

355
00:18:53,625 --> 00:18:57,493
Customers really like him too.

356
00:18:57,516 --> 00:19:01,531
His smile is always so lovely.

357
00:19:01,555 --> 00:19:04,921
He's on the same shift as me tomorrow.

358
00:19:04,944 --> 00:19:07,878
Please teach him all sorts of things.

359
00:19:07,901 --> 00:19:11,956
Yes, I'll teach him kindly.

360
00:19:11,979 --> 00:19:14,990
How old is Suzuki?

361
00:19:15,014 --> 00:19:17,980
He's a 20-year-old university student.

362
00:19:18,003 --> 00:19:20,420
He's so young.

363
00:19:20,444 --> 00:19:23,311
His future looks promising.

364
00:19:23,334 --> 00:19:27,301
Things are going to get busy, so I'm looking forward to it.

365
00:19:27,324 --> 00:19:30,823
Let's all support and help him grow.

366
00:19:40,482 --> 00:19:41,982
Scene 1: Dealing with Cold Symptoms

367
00:19:41,982 --> 00:19:44,816
Listening Test

368
00:19:44,816 --> 00:19:48,082
What's wrong?

369
00:19:48,082 --> 00:19:52,592
Vましたか = Did you do...?
how / what = どう

370
00:19:52,616 --> 00:19:55,882
Listening Test

371
00:19:55,882 --> 00:19:59,716
You don't look well.

372
00:19:59,716 --> 00:20:04,982
いAい + ですよ = It is... (informing)
complexion / facial expression = 顔色(かおいろ)

373
00:20:05,005 --> 00:20:08,672
Listening Test

374
00:20:08,672 --> 00:20:12,980
I'm not feeling too great.

375
00:20:12,980 --> 00:20:18,913
いAくない + んです = It is not... (explaining reason)
feeling / mood = 気分(きぶん)

376
00:20:18,936 --> 00:20:21,444
Listening Test

377
00:20:21,444 --> 00:20:24,311
Are you okay?

378
00:20:24,311 --> 00:20:28,310
なA + ですか = Are you...?
okay / alright = 大丈夫(だいじょうぶ)

379
00:20:28,333 --> 00:20:31,233
Listening Test

380
00:20:31,233 --> 00:20:34,586
Do you have a fever?

381
00:20:34,586 --> 00:20:39,226
N + はありますか = Do you have N?
fever / heat = 熱(ねつ)

382
00:20:39,249 --> 00:20:42,625
Listening Test

383
00:20:42,625 --> 00:20:46,569
I don't think I have a fever.

384
00:20:46,569 --> 00:20:52,004
Vない + と 思(おも)います = I think that... not...
to think = 思(おも)う

385
00:20:52,028 --> 00:20:56,561
Listening Test

386
00:20:56,561 --> 00:21:01,952
But my head is pounding.

387
00:21:01,952 --> 00:21:09,304
N + がします = to feel / smell / sound like N
head = 頭(あたま)
pounding / throbbing = ガンガン

388
00:21:09,328 --> 00:21:12,232
Listening Test

389
00:21:12,232 --> 00:21:15,589
That sounds rough.

390
00:21:15,589 --> 00:21:20,261
なA + ですね = That sounds...
tough / terrible = 大変(たいへん)

391
00:21:20,285 --> 00:21:23,477
Listening Test

392
00:21:23,477 --> 00:21:27,214
You might have a cold.

393
00:21:27,214 --> 00:21:32,356
N + かもしれませんよ = It might be N (informing)
cold (illness) = 風邪(かぜ)

394
00:21:32,379 --> 00:21:35,446
Listening Test

395
00:21:35,446 --> 00:21:38,979
Maybe so.

396
00:21:38,979 --> 00:21:43,857
そう + かもしれません = That might be so
so / like that = そう

397
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:47,947
Listening Test

398
00:21:47,947 --> 00:21:52,735
I've felt a bit chilly since yesterday.

399
00:21:52,735 --> 00:21:59,268
いAかった + です = It was...
yesterday = 昨日(きのう)
cold ↔ hot = 寒(さむ)い ↔ 暑(あつ)い

400
00:21:59,291 --> 00:22:02,825
Listening Test

401
00:22:02,825 --> 00:22:06,960
You should take a rest.

402
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:12,638
Vた + 方(ほう)がいいですよ = You'd better... (e.g., 'You'd better rest.')
休む = to rest / to take time off

403
00:22:12,661 --> 00:22:14,694
Okay.

404
00:22:14,717 --> 00:22:19,017
Listening Test

405
00:22:19,017 --> 00:22:24,117
But I feel dizzy when I stand up.

406
00:22:24,117 --> 00:22:31,064
Vると = when / if V... (e.g., 'When you stand up, you feel dizzy.')
立ち上がる = to stand up
フラフラ = dizzy / unsteady

407
00:22:31,088 --> 00:22:33,921
Listening Test

408
00:22:33,921 --> 00:22:37,188
Don't push yourself.

409
00:22:37,188 --> 00:22:41,688
Vないで + ください = Please don’t... (e.g., 'Please don’t overdo it.')
無理 = overdoing it / impossible

410
00:22:41,711 --> 00:22:46,744
Listening Test

411
00:22:46,744 --> 00:22:52,777
Shall I get you some medicine?

412
00:22:52,777 --> 00:23:00,962
Vましょうか = Shall I...? (e.g., 'Shall I bring you some medicine?')
薬 = medicine
持つ = to hold / to carry

413
00:23:00,986 --> 00:23:03,086
Listening Test

414
00:23:03,086 --> 00:23:05,423
I'm sorry to trouble you.

415
00:23:08,712 --> 00:23:11,579
Listening Test

416
00:23:11,579 --> 00:23:14,889
Here you go.

417
00:23:14,889 --> 00:23:19,522
Here you go.

418
00:23:19,545 --> 00:23:22,615
Listening Test

419
00:23:22,615 --> 00:23:26,182
I'll leave some water here too.

420
00:23:26,182 --> 00:23:31,115
N + も + Vますね = I’ll also do N (e.g., 'I’ll also bring some water.')
水 = water
置く = to put / to place

421
00:23:31,138 --> 00:23:33,289
Listening Test

422
00:23:33,289 --> 00:23:35,723
Thank you.

423
00:23:35,723 --> 00:23:39,117
Thank you very much.

424
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:41,573
Listening Test

425
00:23:41,573 --> 00:23:44,308
That really helps.

426
00:23:44,308 --> 00:23:48,103
Vます = to be helped / to be saved (e.g., 'I’d be so helped!')
助かる = to be saved / to be helped

427
00:23:48,127 --> 00:23:51,765
Listening Test

428
00:23:51,765 --> 00:23:56,065
Anywhere else hurting?

429
00:23:56,065 --> 00:24:01,932
いAい + N = ...N (e.g., 'other painful spots')
他 = other / else
痛い = painful / hurting

430
00:24:01,955 --> 00:24:06,821
Listening Test

431
00:24:06,821 --> 00:24:12,655
Actually, my tooth is throbbing a bit too.

432
00:24:12,655 --> 00:24:20,557
N + も + Vます = N also does... (e.g., 'I also have a cavity that’s throbbing.')
虫歯 = cavity / decayed tooth
ズキズキ = throbbing pain

433
00:24:20,580 --> 00:24:23,576
Listening Test

434
00:24:23,576 --> 00:24:27,054
That must be tough.

435
00:24:27,054 --> 00:24:31,887
いAい + ですね = That is... (e.g., 'That sounds really tough.')
つらい = painful / tough

436
00:24:31,910 --> 00:24:35,456
Listening Test

437
00:24:35,456 --> 00:24:39,627
You should see a dentist too.

438
00:24:39,627 --> 00:24:45,361
Vた + 方(ほう)がいいですよ = You’d better... (e.g., 'You’d better go to the dentist.')
歯医者 = dentist
行く (to go) ↔ 来る (to come)

439
00:24:45,384 --> 00:24:47,981
Listening Test

440
00:24:47,981 --> 00:24:50,953
You're right.

441
00:24:50,953 --> 00:24:55,086
That’s right. / I agree.

442
00:24:55,109 --> 00:24:59,485
Listening Test

443
00:24:59,485 --> 00:25:04,718
I'll rest this afternoon and go to the hospital.

444
00:25:04,718 --> 00:25:11,818
Vて + Vます = to do V and do V (e.g., 'I’ll go to the clinic in the afternoon.')
午後 (afternoon) ↔ 朝 (morning)
病院 = hospital / clinic

445
00:25:11,841 --> 00:25:15,675
Listening Test

446
00:25:15,675 --> 00:25:20,179
I'll let the manager know for you.

447
00:25:20,179 --> 00:25:26,371
Vて + おきますね = I’ll do V in advance (e.g., 'I’ll let the section manager know in advance.')
課長 = section manager
伝える = to convey / to tell

448
00:25:26,394 --> 00:25:29,094
Listening Test

449
00:25:29,094 --> 00:25:32,198
I'm really sorry about this.

450
00:25:32,198 --> 00:25:36,499
I’m sorry. / I apologize.

451
00:25:36,522 --> 00:25:38,689
Listening Test

452
00:25:38,689 --> 00:25:41,122
Please do.

453
00:25:44,541 --> 00:25:47,374
Listening Test

454
00:25:47,374 --> 00:25:50,641
Don't worry about it.

455
00:25:50,641 --> 00:25:55,141
Vないで + ください = Please don’t... (e.g., 'Please don’t worry about it.')
気にする = to worry about / to care

456
00:25:55,163 --> 00:25:58,597
Listening Test

457
00:25:58,597 --> 00:26:02,630
Health is the most important thing.

458
00:26:02,630 --> 00:26:08,148
N1 + が 一番 + なA + です = N1 is the most... (e.g., 'Health is the most important thing.')
健康 = health
大切 = important / precious

459
00:26:08,172 --> 00:26:10,139
Okay.

460
00:26:10,162 --> 00:26:13,428
Listening Test

461
00:26:13,428 --> 00:26:17,224
Yes, I think I'll be better by tomorrow.

462
00:26:17,224 --> 00:26:22,491
Vと + 思います = I think that... (e.g., 'I think you’ll feel better tomorrow.')
明日 = tomorrow
良くなる = to get better

463
00:26:22,514 --> 00:26:25,781
Listening Test

464
00:26:25,781 --> 00:26:29,575
Shall I call a taxi for you?

465
00:26:29,575 --> 00:26:34,808
Vましょうか = Shall I...? (e.g., 'Shall I call someone for you?')
呼ぶ = to call

466
00:26:34,831 --> 00:26:36,623
Okay.

467
00:26:36,646 --> 00:26:38,804
Listening Test

468
00:26:38,804 --> 00:26:41,238
Please do.

469
00:26:44,658 --> 00:26:48,832
Listening Test

470
00:26:48,832 --> 00:26:53,783
I just ordered one using my smartphone app.

471
00:26:53,783 --> 00:27:00,542
N + で + Vました = did V with N (e.g., 'I just called them now.')
今 = now
呼ぶ = to call

472
00:27:00,566 --> 00:27:02,733
Listening Test

473
00:27:02,733 --> 00:27:05,166
Thank you.

474
00:27:05,166 --> 00:27:08,600
Thank you very much.

475
00:27:08,623 --> 00:27:13,357
Listening Test

476
00:27:13,357 --> 00:27:19,023
It'll be here in about 5 minutes, in front of the office.

477
00:27:19,023 --> 00:27:26,697
N + で + Vますよ = will do in/at N (e.g., 'I’ll do it at the office.')
会社 = company / office
前 (front) ↔ 後ろ (back)

478
00:27:26,721 --> 00:27:29,307
Listening Test

479
00:27:29,307 --> 00:27:32,265
I'll gather my things.

480
00:27:32,265 --> 00:27:36,365
N + を + Vます = to do N (e.g., 'Let me pack your luggage.')
荷物 = luggage / baggage
まとめる = to pack / to put together

481
00:27:36,388 --> 00:27:39,722
Listening Test

482
00:27:39,722 --> 00:27:43,623
Let me carry your bag.

483
00:27:43,623 --> 00:27:48,976
Vますよ = I will do... (e.g., 'I’ll carry your bag.')
鞄 = bag

484
00:27:48,999 --> 00:27:52,966
Listening Test

485
00:27:52,966 --> 00:27:57,666
I'm really sorry for all this trouble.

486
00:27:57,666 --> 00:28:04,100
Really, I appreciate everything. / You’ve done so much for me.

487
00:28:04,124 --> 00:28:08,516
Listening Test

488
00:28:08,516 --> 00:28:13,749
Take care. Get plenty of rest.

489
00:28:13,749 --> 00:28:20,884
Please take care of yourself and rest well.
お大事に = take care of yourself
ゆっくり = slowly / comfortably

490
00:28:20,908 --> 00:28:23,174
Listening Test

491
00:28:23,174 --> 00:28:25,722
Thank you.

492
00:28:25,722 --> 00:28:29,289
Thank you very much.

493
00:28:29,312 --> 00:28:31,892
Listening Test

494
00:28:31,892 --> 00:28:34,844
Excuse me.

495
00:28:34,844 --> 00:28:38,957
Excuse me. / Goodbye.

496
00:28:38,981 --> 00:28:40,481
Scene 2: Wrapping Up Work and Dinner Plans

497
00:28:40,481 --> 00:28:45,027
Listening Test

498
00:28:45,027 --> 00:28:50,460
We're done with work for today, right?

499
00:28:50,460 --> 00:28:57,832
N + は + N + で + 終わりました = finished with... (e.g., 'I finished work for today.')
仕事 = work
終わる = to finish

500
00:28:57,856 --> 00:29:01,289
Listening Test

501
00:29:01,289 --> 00:29:05,278
Yes, I'm exhausted.

502
00:29:05,278 --> 00:29:10,778
I got so tired...

503
00:29:10,801 --> 00:29:14,115
Listening Test

504
00:29:14,115 --> 00:29:17,989
I'm completely wiped out.

505
00:29:17,989 --> 00:29:23,322
N + が + くたくたです = ...is exhausted (e.g., 'My body is completely exhausted.')
体 = body
くたくた = exhausted

506
00:29:23,345 --> 00:29:26,537
Listening Test

507
00:29:26,537 --> 00:29:30,251
We walked a lot today.

508
00:29:30,251 --> 00:29:35,369
Vました + から = because... (e.g., 'I’m exhausted because I walked so much.')
歩く = to walk

509
00:29:35,393 --> 00:29:38,378
Listening Test

510
00:29:38,378 --> 00:29:41,847
We sure did.

511
00:29:41,847 --> 00:29:46,627
That’s really true, isn’t it?

512
00:29:46,650 --> 00:29:50,184
Listening Test

513
00:29:50,184 --> 00:29:54,317
My feet are killing me.

514
00:29:54,317 --> 00:30:00,017
いA + いです = is... (e.g., 'My legs are really sore.')
足 = leg, foot
痛い = painful

515
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:05,144
Listening Test

516
00:30:05,144 --> 00:30:11,248
Would you like to grab dinner together later?

517
00:30:11,248 --> 00:30:19,581
Vに + 行きませんか = Won’t you go to do...? (e.g., 'Won’t you go for dinner after this?')
後 = after
晩ご飯 = dinner

518
