758
00:47:48,163 --> 00:47:52,038
Did you contact your friend?

759
00:47:52,038 --> 00:47:57,371
Nに + 連絡しましたか = Did you contact N?
Example: 連絡する = to contact

760
00:47:57,394 --> 00:47:59,148
Okay.

761
00:47:59,171 --> 00:48:02,483
Listening Test

762
00:48:02,483 --> 00:48:06,355
I just sent them a message.

763
00:48:06,355 --> 00:48:11,704
Nを + 送りました = sent N
Example: 送る = to send

764
00:48:11,728 --> 00:48:15,271
Listening Test

765
00:48:15,271 --> 00:48:19,428
What did they say?

766
00:48:19,428 --> 00:48:25,161
何と + 言っていましたか = What did they say?

767
00:48:25,184 --> 00:48:29,584
Listening Test

768
00:48:29,584 --> 00:48:34,817
They said they’d go ahead and get into the theater.

769
00:48:34,817 --> 00:48:41,951
Vる + と + 言っていました = said they would do...
Example: 先に = ahead / first

770
00:48:41,975 --> 00:48:45,208
Listening Test

771
00:48:45,208 --> 00:48:48,942
Was it a movie you were really looking forward to?

772
00:48:48,942 --> 00:48:54,097
Vていた + N = N that was being done
Example: 楽しみ = looking forward to

773
00:48:54,120 --> 00:48:56,154
Okay.

774
00:48:56,177 --> 00:48:59,923
Listening Test

775
00:48:59,923 --> 00:49:04,357
It’s an action movie I’ve been wanting to see for ages.

776
00:49:04,357 --> 00:49:10,423
Vたかった + N = N that I wanted to do
Example: ずっと = all the time

777
00:49:10,446 --> 00:49:15,230
Listening Test

778
00:49:15,230 --> 00:49:20,964
It’s disappointing that you’ll miss the beginning.

779
00:49:20,964 --> 00:49:28,754
Vる + ことができない = cannot do...
Example: ガッカリする = to be disappointed

780
00:49:28,777 --> 00:49:32,157
Listening Test

781
00:49:32,157 --> 00:49:36,124
It’s really too bad.

782
00:49:36,124 --> 00:49:41,591
本当(ほんとう)に = really
Example: 残念 = disappointing / unfortunate

783
00:49:41,614 --> 00:49:45,350
Listening Test

784
00:49:45,350 --> 00:49:49,783
When’s the next train coming?

785
00:49:49,783 --> 00:49:55,850
いつ + Vる + でしょうか = When will... happen, I wonder?

786
00:49:55,873 --> 00:49:59,941
Listening Test

787
00:49:59,941 --> 00:50:04,774
The board doesn’t say.

788
00:50:04,774 --> 00:50:11,407
Vても = even if...
Example: 掲示板 = display board

789
00:50:11,430 --> 00:50:15,164
Listening Test

790
00:50:15,164 --> 00:50:19,598
Should we ask the station attendant?

791
00:50:19,598 --> 00:50:25,631
Vに + 行きましょうか = Shall we go to do...?
Example: 駅員 = station staff

792
00:50:25,654 --> 00:50:27,590
You're right.

793
00:50:27,613 --> 00:50:31,280
Listening Test

794
00:50:31,280 --> 00:50:35,594
There’s one over there.

795
00:50:35,594 --> 00:50:41,527
Nが + います = There is N (animate)

796
00:50:41,550 --> 00:50:44,330
Listening Test

797
00:50:44,330 --> 00:50:47,563
I’ll go ask.

798
00:50:47,563 --> 00:50:52,030
Vてきます = go and do...
Example: ちょっと = a moment

799
00:50:52,053 --> 00:50:54,686
Listening Test

800
00:50:54,686 --> 00:50:57,720
What did they say?

801
00:50:57,720 --> 00:51:01,879
どうでしたか = How was it?

802
00:51:01,903 --> 00:51:06,177
Listening Test

803
00:51:06,177 --> 00:51:11,253
They said it’ll start moving in about 10 minutes.

804
00:51:11,253 --> 00:51:18,186
V始める = start to do...

805
00:51:18,209 --> 00:51:21,109
Listening Test

806
00:51:21,109 --> 00:51:24,462
That’s a relief.

807
00:51:24,462 --> 00:51:29,095
それなら = if so / in that case

808
00:51:29,118 --> 00:51:32,618
Listening Test

809
00:51:32,618 --> 00:51:36,718
Does that ease your mind a little?

810
00:51:36,718 --> 00:51:42,351
モヤモヤする = feeling hazy / uneasy
Example: 晴れる = to clear up

811
00:51:42,374 --> 00:51:44,478
Okay.

812
00:51:44,502 --> 00:51:47,135
Listening Test

813
00:51:47,135 --> 00:51:50,168
Yeah, I feel a bit better now.

814
00:51:50,168 --> 00:51:54,338
安心する = to be relieved

815
00:51:54,362 --> 00:51:58,266
Listening Test

816
00:51:58,266 --> 00:52:02,899
Hope you enjoy the movie!

817
00:52:02,899 --> 00:52:09,203
Vてください = Please do...
Example: 楽しむ = to enjoy

818
00:52:09,227 --> 00:52:11,460
Listening Test

819
00:52:11,460 --> 00:52:13,971
Thank you.

820
00:52:17,511 --> 00:52:20,267
Listening Test

821
00:52:20,267 --> 00:52:23,441
I’m off!

822
00:52:23,441 --> 00:52:27,840
行ってきます = I'm off / See you later

823
00:52:27,864 --> 00:52:29,364
Scene 5: Winter Vacation Travel Plans

824
00:52:29,364 --> 00:52:33,430
Listening Test

825
00:52:33,430 --> 00:52:38,264
Winter break starts tomorrow!

826
00:52:38,264 --> 00:52:44,842
明日から = starting tomorrow
Example: 冬休み = winter break

827
00:52:44,865 --> 00:52:48,815
Listening Test

828
00:52:48,815 --> 00:52:53,481
Yes, I can't wait!

829
00:52:53,481 --> 00:52:59,851
待ち遠しい = can't wait / eagerly awaited

830
00:52:59,874 --> 00:53:03,774
Listening Test

831
00:53:03,774 --> 00:53:08,408
Do you have any plans to go somewhere?

832
00:53:08,408 --> 00:53:14,708
Vる + 予定はありますか = Do you have plans to V?
Example: 出かける = go out

833
00:53:14,731 --> 00:53:18,845
Listening Test

834
00:53:18,845 --> 00:53:23,721
I'm going to Hokkaido with my family.

835
00:53:23,721 --> 00:53:30,387
N1 と N2 = N1 and N2 / with N1
Example: 北海道 = Hokkaido

836
00:53:30,410 --> 00:53:34,944
Listening Test

837
00:53:34,944 --> 00:53:40,341
Hokkaido? That sounds amazing!

838
00:53:40,341 --> 00:53:47,698
N + ですか = Is it N?

839
00:53:47,721 --> 00:53:52,688
Listening Test

840
00:53:52,688 --> 00:53:58,621
It's my first time in a snowy place, so I'm really excited.

841
00:53:58,621 --> 00:54:06,688
N + なので = because it is N
Examples: 雪国 = snowy region, ワクワク = excited

842
00:54:06,711 --> 00:54:09,845
Listening Test

843
00:54:09,845 --> 00:54:13,511
It's going to be really cold, though.

844
00:54:13,511 --> 00:54:18,545
いA + ですよ = It is A (informative)
Examples: 暑い (hot) ↔ 寒い (cold)

845
00:54:18,568 --> 00:54:22,034
Listening Test

846
00:54:22,034 --> 00:54:26,101
Did you buy some warm clothes?

847
00:54:26,101 --> 00:54:31,640
いA + 服 = A clothes
Examples: 厚い (thick) ↔ 薄い (thin)

848
00:54:31,664 --> 00:54:36,734
Listening Test

849
00:54:36,734 --> 00:54:42,801
Yes, I got a new warm coat.

850
00:54:42,801 --> 00:54:51,067
Vました = did V
Example: 暖かい = warm

851
00:54:51,090 --> 00:54:56,124
Listening Test

852
00:54:56,124 --> 00:55:02,157
New clothes always make me happy, don't they?

853
00:55:02,157 --> 00:55:10,333
Vる + と = when / if V
Example: ウキウキ = cheerful / excited

854
00:55:10,357 --> 00:55:14,551
Listening Test

855
00:55:14,551 --> 00:55:19,517
Yeah, I can't wait to wear it.

856
00:55:19,517 --> 00:55:26,300
Vたい = want to V
Example: 着る = wear

857
00:55:26,323 --> 00:55:30,305
Listening Test

858
00:55:30,305 --> 00:55:35,014
What are you planning to do in Hokkaido?

859
00:55:35,014 --> 00:55:41,481
N で = in / at N

860
00:55:41,504 --> 00:55:44,804
Listening Test

861
00:55:44,804 --> 00:55:48,671
I'm going to try skiing.

862
00:55:48,671 --> 00:55:53,946
N をする + 予定です = plan to do N
Example: スキー = ski / skiing

863
00:55:53,970 --> 00:55:57,203
Listening Test

864
00:55:57,203 --> 00:56:00,970
Are you good at skiing?

865
00:56:00,970 --> 00:56:06,156
なA + ですか = Is it A?
Examples: 上手 (skillful) ↔ 下手 (unskillful)

866
00:56:06,179 --> 00:56:09,249
Listening Test

867
00:56:09,249 --> 00:56:12,816
Not at all.

868
00:56:12,816 --> 00:56:17,749
ぜんぜん + Vません = cannot V at all
Example: ぜんぜん = not at all

869
00:56:17,773 --> 00:56:20,840
Listening Test

870
00:56:20,840 --> 00:56:24,381
It's my first time.

871
00:56:24,381 --> 00:56:29,281
N の N = N of N
Example: 経験 = experience

872
00:56:29,304 --> 00:56:32,638
Listening Test

873
00:56:32,638 --> 00:56:36,540
I'm sure you'll have a great time.

874
00:56:36,540 --> 00:56:41,892
きっと + いA + ですよ = It will definitely be A
Example: きっと = surely / definitely

875
00:56:41,915 --> 00:56:45,015
Listening Test

876
00:56:45,015 --> 00:56:48,607
The snow is so beautiful, too.

877
00:56:48,607 --> 00:56:53,557
~し = ..., and also...
Example: 綺麗 = beautiful / clean

878
00:56:53,580 --> 00:56:57,280
Listening Test

879
00:56:57,280 --> 00:57:01,614
I also want to try the delicious seafood bowls.

880
00:57:01,614 --> 00:57:07,562
Vたい = want to eat
Example: 海鮮丼 = seafood bowl

881
00:57:07,585 --> 00:57:11,452
Listening Test

882
00:57:11,452 --> 00:57:15,991
The crab and salmon are amazing there.

883
00:57:15,991 --> 00:57:22,224
N1 や N2 = N1, N2, and so on
Examples: カニ = crab, サーモン = salmon

884
00:57:22,247 --> 00:57:27,441
Listening Test

885
00:57:27,441 --> 00:57:33,674
Just talking about it makes me restless—I can't wait to go!

886
00:57:33,674 --> 00:57:42,113
Vて いる だけ で = just by V-ing
Example: ソワソワ = restless / nervous

887
00:57:42,137 --> 00:57:46,803
Listening Test

888
00:57:46,803 --> 00:57:52,348
I can't focus on work at all today.

889
00:57:52,348 --> 00:57:59,896
N に + ぜんぜん + Vできません = cannot V at all on N
Example: 集中 = concentration

890
00:57:59,920 --> 00:58:03,787
Listening Test

891
00:58:03,787 --> 00:58:08,344
Yeah, I keep checking the clock.

892
00:58:08,344 --> 00:58:14,611
N ばかり + Vて しまいます = do nothing but V
Example: 時計 = clock / watch

893
00:58:14,634 --> 00:58:19,100
Listening Test

894
00:58:19,100 --> 00:58:24,405
Did you check your flight ticket yet?

895
00:58:24,405 --> 00:58:31,672
Have you already [V-ed]? (e.g., 'Have you already confirmed your flight?')
- 飛行機 (ひこうき) = airplane
- 確認 (かくにん) = confirmation

896
00:58:31,695 --> 00:58:34,928
Listening Test

897
00:58:34,928 --> 00:58:38,672
Of course, I did.

898
00:58:38,672 --> 00:58:43,839
Of course I [V-ed]! (e.g., 'Of course I booked it!')
- もちろん = of course

899
00:58:43,862 --> 00:58:47,529
Listening Test

900
00:58:47,529 --> 00:58:51,829
Is your hotel reservation all set?

901
00:58:51,829 --> 00:58:57,729
Is [N] also okay? (e.g., 'Is this reservation also okay?')
- 予約 (よやく) = reservation

902
00:58:57,752 --> 00:59:01,452
Listening Test

903
00:59:01,452 --> 00:59:05,793
Yes, everything's perfect.

904
00:59:05,793 --> 00:59:11,746
Everything is [A] (e.g., 'Everything is perfect!')
- 完璧 (かんぺき) = perfect

905
00:59:11,770 --> 00:59:16,003
Listening Test

906
00:59:16,003 --> 00:59:21,002
Don't forget to bring your camera!

907
00:59:21,002 --> 00:59:27,837
Please take it without [V-ing] (e.g., 'Please take the camera without forgetting it.')
- カメラ = camera

908
00:59:27,860 --> 00:59:31,594
Listening Test

909
00:59:31,594 --> 00:59:36,027
I'll take lots of photos with my smartphone.

910
00:59:36,027 --> 00:59:42,060
Using [N] / By means of [N] (e.g., 'Take a picture using this camera.')
- 撮る (とる) = take (a picture)

911
00:59:42,083 --> 00:59:46,117
Listening Test

912
00:59:46,117 --> 00:59:50,873
I'm looking forward to seeing the beautiful pictures.

913
00:59:50,873 --> 00:59:57,379
Looking forward to [N] (e.g., 'I’m looking forward to the trip!')
- 楽しみ (たのしみ) = looking forward to

914
00:59:57,402 --> 01:00:00,735
Listening Test

915
01:00:00,735 --> 01:00:04,635
I'll show you on Monday.

916
01:00:04,635 --> 01:00:10,002
Will [V] on [N] (e.g., 'I’ll see you on Monday!')
- 月曜日 (げつようび) = Monday

917
01:00:10,025 --> 01:00:13,092
Listening Test

918
01:00:13,092 --> 01:00:16,632
Have a safe trip!

919
01:00:16,632 --> 01:00:21,532
Take care and [V] (e.g., 'Take care and have a safe trip!')
- 気をつける (きをつける) = be careful

920
01:00:21,555 --> 01:00:24,121
Listening Test

921
01:00:24,121 --> 01:00:27,055
Thanks, I'll be off now.

922
01:00:31,178 --> 01:00:34,711
Listening Test

923
01:00:34,711 --> 01:00:38,844
I'll bring you back a souvenir.

924
01:00:38,844 --> 01:00:44,511
Go and [V] / Will [V] and come back (e.g., 'I’ll buy a souvenir and come back.')
- お土産 (みやげ) = souvenir

925
01:00:44,534 --> 01:00:46,034
Scene 6: Sleep and Morning Feelings

926
01:00:46,034 --> 01:00:48,867
Listening Test

927
01:00:48,867 --> 01:00:52,138
Good morning.

928
01:00:56,676 --> 01:00:59,443
Listening Test

929
01:00:59,443 --> 01:01:02,623
Good morning.

930
01:01:07,112 --> 01:01:10,986
Listening Test

931
01:01:10,986 --> 01:01:15,557
You're earlier than usual this morning.

932
01:01:15,557 --> 01:01:21,824
Than [N] (e.g., 'Earlier than this morning.')
- 今朝 (けさ) = this morning
- 早い (はやい) (early) ↔ 遅い (おそい) (late)

933
01:01:21,847 --> 01:01:26,347
Listening Test

934
01:01:26,347 --> 01:01:31,702
I went to bed really early yesterday.

935
01:01:31,702 --> 01:01:39,005
Because... (e.g., 'I’m tired because I slept late yesterday.')
- 昨日 (きのう) = yesterday
- 寝る (ねる) (to sleep) ↔ 起きる (おきる) (to wake up)

936
01:01:39,028 --> 01:01:42,418
Listening Test

937
01:01:42,418 --> 01:01:46,403
Did you sleep well?

938
01:01:46,403 --> 01:01:51,870
Can/Could you [V]? (e.g., 'Could you sleep well?')
- ぐっすり = soundly / deeply

939
01:01:51,894 --> 01:01:56,327
Listening Test

940
01:01:56,327 --> 01:02:01,594
Yes, I didn't wake up once until morning.

941
01:02:01,594 --> 01:02:08,827
Not even one [counter]... (e.g., 'I haven’t even tried it once.')
- 一度も (いちども) = not even once

942
01:02:08,850 --> 01:02:12,166
Listening Test

943
01:02:12,166 --> 01:02:16,066
That's great!

944
01:02:16,066 --> 01:02:21,418
Was [A] (e.g., 'It was fun!')

945
01:02:21,442 --> 01:02:26,275
Listening Test

946
01:02:26,275 --> 01:02:32,049
I feel so refreshed this morning.

947
01:02:32,049 --> 01:02:39,916
Thanks to... (e.g., 'Thanks to the good sleep, I feel refreshed.')
- すっきり = refreshed

948
01:02:39,938 --> 01:02:43,124
Listening Test

949
01:02:43,124 --> 01:02:46,840
You look really energetic.

950
01:02:46,840 --> 01:02:51,973
Looks/Seems [na-adjective] (e.g., 'You look energetic!')
- 元気 (げんき) = energetic / healthy

951
01:02:51,996 --> 01:02:56,563
Listening Test

952
01:02:56,563 --> 01:03:01,996
Yeah. You look a bit sleepy, though.

953
01:03:01,996 --> 01:03:09,429
Looks/Seems [i-adjective] (e.g., 'You look sleepy.')
- 眠い (ねむい) = sleepy

954
01:03:09,452 --> 01:03:14,719
Listening Test

955
01:03:14,719 --> 01:03:21,019
Actually, I was playing games late into the night.

956
01:03:21,019 --> 01:03:29,563
Until [N] (e.g., 'Actually, I stayed up late last night.')
- 実は (じつは) = actually / in fact
- 夜遅く (よるおそく) = late at night

957
01:03:29,587 --> 01:03:32,491
Listening Test

958
01:03:32,491 --> 01:03:35,857
How many hours did you sleep?

959
01:03:35,857 --> 01:03:40,524
How many [units]? (e.g., 'How many hours did you sleep?')
- 何時間 (なんじかん) = how many hours

960
01:03:40,547 --> 01:03:43,980
Listening Test

961
01:03:43,980 --> 01:03:48,014
About three hours.

962
01:03:48,014 --> 01:03:53,547
About [quantity] (e.g., 'It took about three hours.')
- くらい = about / approximately

963
01:03:53,570 --> 01:03:56,870
Listening Test

964
01:03:56,870 --> 01:04:00,737
That's way too little!

965
01:04:00,737 --> 01:04:06,037
Too [i-adjective] (e.g., 'This is too short!')
- 短い (みじかい) (short) ↔ 長い (ながい) (long)

966
01:04:06,060 --> 01:04:08,560
Listening Test

967
01:04:08,560 --> 01:04:11,427
It's bad for your health.

968
01:04:11,427 --> 01:04:15,380
Bad for [N] (e.g., 'Staying up late is bad for your health.')
- 体 (からだ) = body / health
- 悪い (わるい) (bad) ↔ 良い (よい) (good)

969
01:04:15,403 --> 01:04:20,470
Listening Test

970
01:04:20,470 --> 01:04:26,536
Yeah, I dozed off during the meeting earlier.

971
01:04:26,536 --> 01:04:34,770
During [N] (e.g., 'I dozed off during the meeting.')
- うとうとする = to doze off

972
01:04:34,793 --> 01:04:37,499
Listening Test

973
01:04:37,499 --> 01:04:40,610
Really?

974
01:04:40,610 --> 01:04:44,943
Really / Truth (e.g., 'Is that really true?')
- 本当 (ほんとう) = really / truth

975
01:04:44,966 --> 01:04:48,299
Listening Test

976
01:04:48,299 --> 01:04:52,199
Did the manager notice?

977
01:04:52,199 --> 01:04:57,554
Passive [V] (e.g., 'The report was scolded by the section chief.')
- 課長 (かちょう) = section chief

978
01:04:57,578 --> 01:05:01,412
Listening Test

979
01:05:01,412 --> 01:05:05,916
I think it was probably okay.

980
01:05:05,916 --> 01:05:12,094
I think that... (e.g., 'I think it’ll probably be okay.')
- 多分 (たぶん) = probably / maybe
- 大丈夫 (だいじょうぶ) = okay / all right

981
01:05:12,117 --> 01:05:15,593
Listening Test

982
01:05:15,593 --> 01:05:19,664
You should be careful, though.

983
01:05:19,664 --> 01:05:25,258
Had better [V] (e.g., 'You’d better be careful.')
- 気を付ける (きをつける) = to be careful

984
01:05:25,281 --> 01:05:30,315
Listening Test

985
01:05:30,315 --> 01:05:36,348
I want to go home early after work today.

986
01:05:36,348 --> 01:05:44,526
After/When [V] (e.g., 'Let’s go home after finishing this.')
